      "title": "H3 edit prompt | OUTFIT SWAP | Universal 16",
      "properties": {
        "cnr_id": "comfy-core",
        "ver": "0.45.0",
        "Node name for S&R": "MiniMaxH3ImageConditioning"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "Edit <Picture 1>. Replace the MAIN PERSON and the complete visible outfit with the person shown in <Picture 2>.\n\n<Picture 1> determines the scene, camera perspective, exact location of the person, original action, body pose, framing, environment and lighting. <Picture 2> determines the replacement character: recognizable facial identity, head, hairstyle, physique, visible clothing, original clothing colors, textures and accessories.\n\nRecreate the person from <Picture 2> in the original person’s position and pose, with natural anatomy, perspective, lighting, occlusion and shadows.\n\nKeep the exact framing and composition of <Picture 1>. Replace only the visible portion of the person within the original photograph. Do not expand the framing, reveal additional body parts, change the camera distance, or turn a portrait into a full-body image.\n\nPreserve the actual clothing visible in <Picture 2>, including its original colors, patterns and fabric appearance. Do not inherit clothing or clothing colors from the person in <Picture 1>, and do not invent a different outfit.\n\nLeave all other people, props and the background of <Picture 1> unchanged. The original person’s head, hair and visible clothing should not remain. Do not create a hybrid of the two people or copy the background of <Picture 2>.",
        2048,
        2048
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "prompt": "Edit <Picture 1>. Replace the MAIN PERSON and the complete visible outfit with the person shown in <Picture 2>.\n\n<Picture 1> determines the scene, camera perspective, exact location of the person, original action, body pose, framing, environment and lighting. <Picture 2> determines the replacement character: recognizable facial identity, head, hairstyle, physique, visible clothing, original clothing colors, textures and accessories.\n\nRecreate the person from <Picture 2> in the original person’s position and pose, with natural anatomy, perspective, lighting, occlusion and shadows.\n\nKeep the exact framing and composition of <Picture 1>. Replace only the visible portion of the person within the original photograph. Do not expand the framing, reveal additional body parts, change the camera distance, or turn a portrait into a full-body image.\n\nPreserve the actual clothing visible in <Picture 2>, including its original colors, patterns and fabric appearance. Do not inherit clothing or clothing colors from the person in <Picture 1>, and do not invent a different outfit.\n\nLeave all other people, props and the background of <Picture 1> unchanged. The original person’s head, hair and visible clothing should not remain. Do not create a hybrid of the two people or copy the background of <Picture 2>.",
        "width": 2048,
        "height": 2048
